! The E-Jing-A-Ling Thing ~ readings handle

''Sixty-four hexagrams and `000pi`, one reading each.'' The 23ae.com page took the I Ching and
"created Discordian answers that had some similarity to the Chinese meanings"; its authors name
themselves only as "we". Each reading rests as its own tiddler beside this handle
(`hexagram-01` through `hexagram-64`, and `hexagram-pi` for a coin that lands on its edge), with
its `source`, `source-sha256`, `license` and `attribution` fields, and the figure bottom line first
in `lines` (1 for yang). The page draws hexagrams 23, 36 and 37 with the figures of 29, 35 and 36; those
three readings keep the page's drawing in `page-lines` beside the King Wen figure. The DOA readings (oracles/doa) carry the same prose under the AppleKatation's
own Kopyleft.

A house cast (`lares oracle cast`) names the readings of the hexagrams it lands on. The oracle widens
attention and never decides.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/provenance`>>

!! Provenance & License

* ''Source:'' "E-Jing-A-Ling Thing Hexagrams", 23ae.com, as the Wayback Machine captured it on
  2006-02-18; the oracle scout carried the page in once (111,063 bytes, sha256
  `d1a27264fae6598cc29ef44cf2c1fd5a7858534fd91f1122538b3ddf9527746e`), and the import read those
  bytes. No reader fetches the web2 page again.
* ''License, the page's own prose:'' "(K)opyLeft: Copyright Is Reversed. Reprint What You Like."
  (hexagram 14).
* ''The quoted snippets:'' the page quotes others inside its readings (the Principia Discordia, Joyce,
  a sutta, Bierce, a book review, a Usenet thread, and more). They ride under fair use by the
  operator's ruling of 2026-11-20 ("Combined with discordian i-ching readings enacts the transformative
  gate"), each quote sitting inside its reading with the attribution the page gives it.
* ''The method the page teaches:'' think of a question and flip a coin six times, heads for yang and
  tails for yin, reading the figure from the bottom up. The house's own cast throws three coins a line
  (6, 7, 8, 9), so a line can change.

<<~/ahu>>

